Tracked announcements (`data/*.json`)
-------------------------------------
Each event records a public announcement made by someone else: a post by a
vendor account or an employee, a changelog entry, a status page note. Rows
carry the announcement's own text, its author, its timestamp and a link back to
the original.

That text is quoted, not licensed. Copyright in each announcement stays with
whoever wrote it. It is reproduced here in short excerpts, attributed and
linked to the source, so that a factual record of when limits moved can be
checked against its origin. Anyone reusing this dataset is responsible for
their own basis for quoting the underlying posts.

Requests to correct or remove a specific quoted announcement are welcome
through the contact route on the maintainer's site.

Own-account measurements (`data/observed/`, when present)
---------------------------------------------------------
Readings of the maintainer's own subscription quota, taken from vendor APIs
with that account's own credentials. These are original observations and are
covered by the MIT licence with the rest of the project. They are not vendor
telemetry and say nothing about any other account.
